{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1320203-the-pack-101-packs","id":1320203,"title":"[The Pack] 101 Packs","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-06-22T22:22:55-07:00","id":1320203,"title":"[The Pack] 101 Packs","content":"We have topics about story ideas, spirits and even particular werewolves. But we still do not have topic for collecting ideas for Packs. So here you got one. Only restriction is that we use <i>Pack as Character</i> structure from <b>The Pack</b> sourcebook for <b>WtF</b> 2E. ( Most you need to know is in the template of my own write-up. ) Other forumers can help you hammer needed Pack elements if you ask nicely. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> In next post will be mine Predator Kings pack write-up that follows ancient cave bear Totem. I will edit it when adding next elements to this pack. Comments are welcome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-22T22:23:53-07:00","id":1320204,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:24px\"><b>1 - \u2018Bear Growl\u2019 Pack</b></span><br /> <br /> This is cave bear primitives cult run by Predator Kings under patronage of cave bear Totem. Think of them as Wendols from <b>13<sup>th</sup> Warrior</b> movie or <b>Eaters of Dead</b> book. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Pack is stealing human children and raise them \u2018as bears\u2019 in the caves that are heart of it\u2019s territory.<br /> <br /> <b>Pack Aspirations:</b><br /> <br /> Short-Term \u2013 Raid human settlements<br /> Medium-Term \u2013 Clean area of Forsaken werewolves<br /> Long-Term \u2013 Restore the cave bears to being - May try breeding of brown bears or possessing by their Totem, for example<br /> <br /> <b>Pack Touchstones:</b><br /> <br /> Physical \u2013 \u2018Den\u2019 of pack, previous cave bears cave<br /> Spiritual \u2013 Skull of the Totems original ( see below )<br /> <br /> <b>Pack Complications:</b><br /> <br /> Stone Age Culture \u2013 Pack members are living like humans before any technology beside stone and bones tools.<br /> <br /> <b>Hunting Nature: </b>Wolf<br /> <br /> <b>Pack Merits:</b><br /> Den \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2013 \u2018Bear\u2019s Den\u2019, cave system<br /> Directed Rage \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> Magnanimous Totem \u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> Territorial Advantage \u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> <br /> <b>Secondary Packmembers</b><br /> <br /> ( Standard are 5/4/3 pools, but I changed them because of this packs profile. )<br /> <br /> Physical: 6<br /> Social: 4<br /> Mental: 2<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Totem: Paw in Darkness</b></span><br /> <br /> &lt;Echo of roar of the raged bear in cave&gt;<br /> <b>Totem Type:</b> Hunting Bear Spirit ( Cave Bear )<br /> <b>Totem Rank: </b>4<br /> <b>Background:</b> Paw is prehistoric being, first created when Neanderthals killed local cave bears colony. By death of biggest male, the spirit awoken, taking it\u2019s form. It\u2019s survived and roused in power when first humans took the bones and relicts from its physical bodies, starting to worship it as ancient primordial god. In a year or two, first local Uratha that later become Predator Kings found the spirit \u2013 and sign the bloody compact. Werewolves will bring the spiritual hunting offerings to Paw, and it will grant \u2018the might of 10 bears\u2019 for them. It\u2019s the same now from the millennia. Pure kidnap humans and Wolf-Blooded to run primitive cult in caves nearby that\u2019s worship generate Essence for the Paw to survive all this years. Spirit lord also guide and watch over local brown bears population, like his own grandchildren.<br /> <br /> <b>Description: </b>Paw physically is great cave bear male \u2013 looking like weighting over 500 kg - only shrouded in darkness ( like permanent shadow ) and dirty in blood of it\u2019s victims.<br /> <br /> <b>Storytelling Hints:</b> Paw understand that time of his kind is over. He is using Pure and humans as Essence generators, but in secret he loathes them. However, he is not stupid and knows that without constant spring of worship, he would perish quickly. He then transfer his inner rage on the civilized settlements of humans he destroys with his Uratha adopted children.<br /> <br /> <b>Aspirations:</b><br /> To resurrect glory of bear-kind<br /> Destroy human civilization<br /> <br /> <b>Rank:</b> 4<br /> <b>Attributes:</b> Power 12, Finesse 8, Resistance 10<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 10<br /> <b>Essence:</b> 25<br /> <b>Initiative: </b>18<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 8<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 25<br /> <b>Size:</b> 10<br /> <b>Corpus:</b> 20<br /> <b>Influences:</b> Bear \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Hunting \u2022\u2022\u2022, Darkness \u2022\u2022<br /> <b>Manifestations:</b> Gauntlet Breach, Image, Materialize, Posses, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina:</b> Awe, Blast (Claw marks on victim ), Host Jump, Might*, Pathfinder, Regenerate, Shadow Form**<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Cannot rest in man-made den ( Paw is nocturnal creature of darkness - and Helios make Shadow Realm more dormant in day - so rest means in the light of day hours. Thanks <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a> for that idea! ) <br /> <b>Bane:</b> Stone weapons of the Neatherdals that killed it\u2019s physical original<br /> <br /> <b>New Numina</b><br /> <br /> <b>Might</b><br /> Spirit can blessed itself \u2013 or other being it is touching \u2013 with supernatural strength. After activating power with touch, next roll based on Strength or Power of the target use this trait multiplied by the Rank of spirit. Each blessing costs 3 Essence and takes one action of the spirit if made on other being. If spirit is Totem for the pack, it can bless pack members from the other side.<br /> <br /> <b>Shadow Form</b><br /> Spirit can take form of living shadow, indistinguishable from normal lights effect. It became two dimensional and moves on any surface just like shadow could. Change cost 1 Essence and is instant. Change back to more physical form cost the same.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Uratha</b></span><br /> <br /> Alpha<br /> Seer<br /> Tracker<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Wolf-Blooded</b></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <a href=\"https://i.pinimg.com/originals/ca/bd/4a/cabd4ae22fc2ef5d0c1eff56d0eb2f8b.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://i.pinimg.com/originals/ca/bd/4a/cabd4ae22fc2ef5d0c1eff56d0eb2f8b.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a><br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":".  Added Ban section to Totem write-up 06-24-2019, 10:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-03T03:20:47-07:00","id":1322002,"title":"","content":"Here is Alpha King of the Pack in the caves - comments are welcomed here. If finalized, I will post him to main post. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Ban (from Totem):</b></span> <i>Cannot rest in man-made den - </i>Paw in Darkness is nocturnal creature of dark - and Helios make Shadow Realm more dormant in day - so for pack rest means in the light of day hours. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Alpha &lt; In First Tongue &gt;</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Blood: </b>Alpha<br /> <b>Bone: </b>Role Model<br /> <b>Tribe:</b> Predator Kings<br /> <b>Attributes: </b>Intelligence 3, Wits 4, Resolve 4, Strength 4 (5/6/5/4), Dexterity 3 (3/4/5/5), Stamina 4 (5/6/6/5), Presence 4, Manipulation 3 (2/3/2/2), Composure 3<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Crafts 3, Investigation 2, Occult 2, Politics 2, Athletics 4, Brawl ( Claws ) 4, Larceny 2, Stealth 4, Survival 5, Weaponry ( Bones ) 4, Animal Ken (Bears) 3, Empathy 2, Intimidation 4, Persuasion 1, Streetwise 2 - Animal Ken, Crafts, and Survival<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Fast Reflexes 3, Favored Form (Dalu) 1, Fortified Form (Dalu) 4, Grappling 3, Iron Stamina 3, Living Weapon (Dalu) 3, Patient 1, Spiritual Blockage 2, Totem 3<br /> <b>Primal Urge:</b> 3<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 7<br /> <b>Harmony:</b> 3 ( Bans \u2013 Cannot sleep in night, Cannot use man-made weapons )<br /> <b>Essence:</b> 12<br /> <b>Health:</b> 9 (12/14/13/10)<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 10 (10/11/12/12)<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 7 (7/7/7/7)<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 12 (13/16/19/17)<br /> <b>Renown:</b> Glory 4, Purity 3, Wisdom 2<br /> <b>Gifts:</b> Nature, Rage, Stealth, and Strength \u2013 <b>Nature: </b>Black Earth, Red Hunger (Glory \u2013 Controlling vines ), Pack Kin (Purity \u2013 \u2018Charming\u2019 animals, often used on Bears), Beast Ride (Wisdom \u2013 controlling animals, often used on Bears); <b>Rage:</b> Berserker\u2019s Might (Glory \u2013 Miss 1/turn Glory in damage ), Slaughterer (Purity \u2013 Adding Purity to Brawl damage in Gauru), Raging Lunacy (Wisdom \u2013 Sure Berseker Lunacy in witness); <b>Stealth:</b> Predator\u2019s Shadow (Glory \u2013 Shadow Paranoia on target on success ), Running Silent (Wisdom \u2013 Stealth even on running, omits Wisdom penalties by terrain); <b>Strength:</b> Primal Strength (Purity \u2013 Adds Purity to Strength rolls), Rending Claws (Wisdom \u2013 Adds Wisdom damage by claws or jaws on Structure )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-08T07:41:37-07:00","id":1322964,"title":"","content":"I did a brief writeup of what the main cast of characters (a college hockey team) of the web comic &quot;Check Please!&quot; would look like as a Werewolf Pack.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://solidork.tumblr.com/post/183129251817/smh-as-a-werewolf-pack\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://solidork.tumblr.com/post/183129251817/smh-as-a-werewolf-pack\" target=\"_blank\"> Not found. </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://solidork.tumblr.com/post/183129251817/smh-as-a-werewolf-pack\" target=\"_blank\"> https://solidork.tumblr.com/post/183129251817/smh-as-a-werewolf-pack </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","name":"solidork","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-14T10:40:16-08:00","id":1348517,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:24px\"><b>2 - \u2018VIP Experiences Inc.\u2019 Pack</b></span><br /> <br /> <br /> This is a now human cult, a Storm Lord pack that was wiped out by conflict with the Pure. Lacking Uratha guidance, the totem is driving the human and wolf-blooded members toward a maddening behaviour. The Mystery Cult ended up attracting a possessor Lust spirit; the original Pack rescued them as part of the process of bringing the Totem to heel.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Pack Aspirations:</b><br /> Short-Term \u2013 Indulge desires, specially those of a sexual nature.<br /> Medium-Term \u2013 Expand the ranks of the pack.<br /> Long-Term \u2013 None, lack of purpose is the worst part of losing the Uratha. Zia has a vague hint of what it wants but nothing it has shared with the cult.<br /> <br /> <b>Pack Touchstones:</b><br /> Physical \u2013 A sex-club in a discrete neighborhood. Here the cult activities take place.<br /> Spiritual \u2013 A lock of braided hair, the main symbol used to bind Zia in service to the original pack.<br /> <br /> <b>Pack Complications:</b><br /> No goals \u2013 Pack members are living day to day, nearly like junkies, focused on the next orgy or encounter.<br /> Old habits \u2013 The current Pack leader is the former assistant of the founder of the Mystery Cult. She has grown the cult repeating the things her master did (enhanced by the Totem powers) but these activities will soon attract notice.<br /> <br /> <b>Hunting Nature: </b><br /> Human<br /> <br /> <b>Pack Merits:</b><br /> Magnanimous Totem 4<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Totem: Zia, Overwhelming Passion</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Totem Type:</b> Lust Spirit<br /> <b>Totem Rank: </b>3<br /> <b>Background:</b> Zia was born of the indulgence of the elite, but it became quite damaging to the humans in the sex-club that it used to inhabit. Brought to heel by the Alpha of the original pack, it survived the pack's destruction by possessing a human host.<br /> <br /> <b>Description: </b>Zia is a pink-reddish translucent bulge of flesh contorted in vaguely suggestive shapes, but can produce male or female genitalia at will.<br /> <br /> <b>Storytelling Hints:</b> Zia wants to use the cult as a recruiting ground for its pack, the more the cult grows (and it is a very attractive proposition to join it), the more Zia's power rises. Zia misses the spiritual component that is lacking in the current configuration of the pack, but finds the Uratha too violent for its tastes. To fulfill that need, it is trying to attract supernatural-touched humans as part of the cult. However, the current human leader of the cult has different expectations of the members, some friction will arise from this.<br /> <br /> <b>Aspirations: </b>Satisfy sexual urges.<br /> <br /> <b>Totem Points:</b> 21<br /> <br /> <b>Rank:</b> 3<br /> <b>Attributes:</b> Power 8, Finesse 8, Resistance 5<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 10<br /> <b>Essence:</b> 20<br /> <b>Initiative: </b>13<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 8<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 21<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5<br /> <b>Corpus:</b> 10<br /> <b>Influences:</b> Lust 3<br /> <b>Manifestations:</b> Twilight Form, Gauntlet Breach, Possess, Claim<br /> <b>Numina:</b> Aggressive Meme, Drain, Emotional Aura, Host Jump, Implant Mission, Rapture<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Zia must be in the presence of someone indulging in lust every 24 hours, otherwise it becomes morose and lethargic losing it\u2019s defense.<br /> <b>Bane:</b> A human that has been voluntarily celibate for a year.<br /> <b>Totem Advantage:</b> Dexterity +1, Stamina +1, Merit: Striking Looks 2<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Mystery Cult Initiation (VIP Experiences Inc.)</b></span><br /> <br /> Entry to the cult has stringent criteria set by the current leader Marina, so there are few cult initiates and even fewer actual pack members among them. The cult offers to connect you with the &quot;In&quot; crowd; but the higher one rises, the more it demands dedication to Zia's aims (at this moment frequent sexual encounters to be feed, and searching for humans with supernatural abilities, which has been unsuccessful due to the lack of mystical talent in the cult).<br /> <br /> <b>Cultists</b>: Former sex worker, vicarious assistant, hopeful starlet, jaded celebrity, aspiring model.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 2px\"><b>Rating</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 2px\"><b>Rank</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 2px\"><b>Description</b> (<i>Shares benefits of the Status Merit)</i></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 2px\">\u2022</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 2px\">Beneficiary</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 2px\">Obtain a Seduction specialty in Persuasion.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 2px\">\u2022\u2022</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 2px\">Personality</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 2px\">Receive the merit Area of Expertise (Seduction).</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 2px\">\u2022\u2022\u2022</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 2px\">Promoter</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 2px\">Gain a dot of Persuasion.<i> Required level to join the pack.</i></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 2px\">\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 2px\">Organizer</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 2px\">Gain the Tell (Exciting) merit.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 2px\">\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 2px\">Influencer</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 2px\">Distribute up to three dots among Fame and Resources.</td> </tr> </table></div> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Alpha </b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Name:</b> Marina Rosa<br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Generous<br /> <b>Vice:</b> Lustful<br /> <b>Aspirations:</b> Become rich; Empower the cult; Find &quot;special people&quot; for Zia; Satisfy sexual urges<br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 2, Wits 4, Resolve 3<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 1, Dexterity 4, Stamina 4<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 4, Manipulation 4, Composure 3<br /> <b>Mental Skills:</b> Academics 1, Computer (Digital Edition) 1, Medicine 1, Occult 3, Politics 1<br /> <b>Physical Skills:</b> Athletics (Workouts) 3, Drive 1<br /> <b>Social Skills: </b>Empathy 3, Expression (Dance, Vlogs) 2, Intimidation 2, Persuasion (Sales Pitches, Seduction) 3, Socialize 3, Subterfuge 3<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Area of Expertise (Seduction), Barfly, Contacts (Actors, Models), Deadpan, Empath, Fame 1, Multilingual (Italian, Portuguese; native Spanish), Mystery Cult Initiation (VIP Experiences Inc) 5, Professional Training (Influencer; Empathy, Expression, Persuasion) 5, Resources 3, Skolis-Ur\u2019s Blood, Striking Looks (Stunning) 2, Tell (Exciting), Totem (Zia) 5<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 6<br /> <b>Integrity: </b>6<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 7<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 8<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 10<br /> <b>Health:</b> 9<br /> <b>Tell:</b> A Wolf\u2019s Meat, Exciting<br /> <b>Conditions:</b> Informed (Werewolves), Resonant (Zia)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 10-25-2026, 08:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-05T21:12:12-07:00","id":1458932,"title":"","content":"<u><i><b>A bit of necromancy but I really like this thread concept and would love to see some pack ideas.</b></i></u><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:24px\"><b>3 - \u2018K4b4l\u2019 Pack</b></span><br /> <br /> An experiment run between the Iron Masters and the Free Council, a hybrid of cabal and pack, more of the latter than the former though.<br /> <br /> <b>Pack Aspirations:</b><br /> Short-Term \u2013 Strengthen the totem.<br /> Medium-Term \u2013 Grow in resources by absorbing the Packs and Cabals of Iron Masters and Free Councillors.<br /> Long-Term \u2013 Transform into a Lodge / Create a Legacy.<br /> <br /> <b>Pack Touchstones:</b><br /> Physical \u2013 A reformed warehouse, fitted with comfortable living quarters and quite secure.<br /> Spiritual \u2013 The server that is KPX\u2019s near permanent fetter.<br /> <br /> <b>Pack Complications:</b><br /> Something to prove \u2013 Can this union work? Especially with limited membership and some traditionalist of each splat opposed to dealing with &quot;others&quot;.<br /> Different objectives \u2013 Iron Masters and Free Councillors have divergent expectations for the experiment, for the werewolves this is a pack that feeds of the mages resonance and resources, for the mages this is an experiment on inter-species cooperation and the potentials of techno-spirituality.<br /> <br /> <b>Hunting Nature: </b><br /> Human<br /> <br /> <b>Pack Merits:</b><br /> Den 5<br /> Safe Place 5<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Totem: KPX</b></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Totem Type:</b> Magath<br /> <b>Totem Rank: </b>1<br /> <b>Background:</b> KPX is a completely artificial spirit, in the sense that it did not appear naturally, but it was created by forcefully mixing diverse resonances associated to computing and finance to create a subservient being.<br /> <br /> <b>Description: </b>A silvered sphere with flashing currency symbols on its surface.<br /> <br /> <b>Storytelling Hints:</b> Mages and Werewolves have different sets of prospects of how this could work, KPX itself is not strong enough to have opinions beyond what its nature demands. Some members think the pack could also transform into a bridge for diverse technology related creatures (things like Unfleshed Prometheans or Demons could fit easily here).<br /> <br /> <b>Aspirations: </b>Make money through IT.<br /> <br /> <b>Totem Points:</b> 5<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Rank:</b> 1<br /> <b>Attributes:</b> Power 2, Finesse 2, Resistance 1<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 3<br /> <b>Essence:</b> 5<br /> <b>Initiative: </b>3<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 2<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 13<br /> <b>Size:</b> 3<br /> <b>Corpus:</b> 4<br /> <b>Influences:</b> Computers 1, Money 1<br /> <b>Manifestations:</b> Twilight Form, Fetter<br /> <b>Numina:</b> Left-Handed Spanner; 1 Numen exchanged for an Influence dot<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Must offer financial or computer advice to anyone who asks.<br /> <b>Bane:</b> Physical currency of any kind.<br /> <b>Conditions: </b>Fettered (Server)<br /> <b>Totem Advantage:</b> Merit: Resources 1<br /> <br /> <br /> (I need help for the Ban and Bane, not sure what to use really).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 09-15-2024, 08:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-07T04:45:48-07:00","id":1459117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1320203-the-pack-101-packs?p=1458932#post1458932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <div align=\"center\">***SNIP***</div> <br /> (I need help for the Ban and Bane, not sure what to use really).</div> </div> </div> </div>Well as a cross splat group, I do think K4b4l can benefit from the Contagion Player's Companion, that wasn't what you asked for.<br /> As an artificial spirit (and/or magrath), KPX doesn't need to have to have a logical Ban or Bane. It is more fun though. Maybe assign one after the computer influence and the other after the finance influence? So if KPX had a Bane of Apple<sup>tm</sup> products, then I'd have the Ban based on something to do with money.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-07T06:31:32-07:00","id":1459132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1320203-the-pack-101-packs?p=1459117#post1459117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well as a cross splat group, I do think K4b4l can benefit from the Contagion Player's Companion, that wasn't what you asked for.<br /> As an artificial spirit (and/or magrath), KPX doesn't need to have to have a logical Ban or Bane. It is more fun though. Maybe assign one after the computer influence and the other after the finance influence? So if KPX had a Bane of Apple<sup>tm</sup> products, then I'd have the Ban based on something to do with money.</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome! Thanks for the ideas, I am considering changing the Ban to computers only aspects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-07T06:51:51-07:00","id":1459133,"title":"","content":"Bane: GPUs burnt out from mining crypto currency?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-07T13:23:08-07:00","id":1459179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1320203-the-pack-101-packs?p=1459133#post1459133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bane: GPUs burnt out from mining crypto currency?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is too specific for a Rank 1 spirit:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BANES</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rank 1 spirits have <b>common substances and phenomena</b><br /> as banes. The spirit of a forest is poisoned by the fumes of<br /> burning plastic.<br /> <br /> Rank 2 and 3 spirits have<b> difficult to obtain but still \u201cnatural\u201d<br /> banes.</b> A wildwood spirit must be killed by a sharpened<br /> stake made of pine.<br /> <br /> Rank 4 and 5 spirits have <b>highly-specific banes that<br /> require great effort to acquire.</b> The spirit of the US Treasury<br /> (the building) can be killed by a silver bullet made from a<br /> melted-down original dollar.</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems very close to the specificity of higher rank spirits. Hell, with the current cost of GPUs and the specific usage that must burn it, this seems something for a Rank 4 spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 09-07-2021, 05:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-24T22:04:38-07:00","id":1523120,"title":"","content":"<u><i><b>More thread necromancy.</b></i></u><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:24px\"><b>4 - \u2018Palisades Park\u2019 Pack</b></span><br /> <br /> This is a generational pack, that has been working with the totem for over 40 years, Iron Masters all of them. They either work at the mall administration, security, or in one of its stores; all Werewolves and some Wolf-Blooded live in the surrounding area. The pack claims the mall itself as territory but also the adjacent high income neighborhood that grew around it.<br /> <br /> <b>Pack Aspirations:</b><br /> Short-Term \u2013 Increase the area security.<br /> Medium-Term \u2013 Relocate the pack members closer to the mall.<br /> Long-Term \u2013 Cater to every need that the people of the area could have (Hotel, Hospital, and Gym are in the roadmap).<br /> <br /> <b>Pack Touchstones:</b><br /> Physical \u2013 The mall (including its fenced parking lot) itself.<br /> Spiritual \u2013 The receipt of first sale made in the mall.<br /> <br /> <b>Pack Complications:</b><br /> Security issues \u2013 Someone entered the mall and killed a pizza parlor dispatcher in a murder-suicide. This rattled customers and businesses both, but how to improve the perception of security without being an obstacle to operations?<br /> Funding \u2013 While quite a prosperous Pack, the expansion plans are very expensive and will tie assets for a while. Shady characters are offering cheap loans but the pack is looking for alternate options.<br /> New homes \u2013 Most, but not all, pack members live within walking distance of the mall; the Pack wants to buy an old residential building in the area to offer cheap housing to their members, but one of the residents is a supernatural that does not want to sell, can he be convinced? Must he be dealt with violence? And how did this guy came to live in their territory without them knowing?<br /> <br /> <b>Hunting Nature: </b><br /> Human<br /> <br /> <b>Pack Merits:</b><br /> Dedicated Locus 5<br /> Den 5<br /> Resources 5<br /> Safe Place 5<br /> Staff 5<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Totem: Palisades, Prosperity Through Commerce</b></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Totem Type:</b> Multiplex Spirit<br /> <b>Totem Rank: </b>3<br /> <b>Background: </b>This is the spirit of the oldest and one of the largest malls in the city. The mall is not in the outskirts, the adjacent high income neighborhoods grew around the mall as part of the effect of its construction.<br /> <br /> <b>Description: </b>A perpetually smiling attractive female made of white plaster dressed in professional attire mounted on (and merged with) a Segway, they have a blinking earpiece, the mall logo instead of irises and every so often they incite the interlocutor to acquire wares or services from the mall.<br /> <br /> <b>Storytelling Hints:</b> The pack has carefully cultivated the influences of the spirit, they want it to embody all the region qualities they like, but not too much of anything. <i>&quot;We want you to be important but not important enough to overshadow us&quot;.</i> So far it has worked because the totem was not self aware enough to aspire more, but the growth in Rank gave a commensurate change in mindset, the Totem aims for higher office and the Borough area spirit seems a very tempting target.<br /> <br /> <b>Aspirations: </b>The mall must grow.<br /> <br /> <b>Totem Points:</b> 21<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Rank</b>: 3<br /> <b>Attributes</b>: Power 6, Finesse 9, Resistance 6<br /> <b>Willpower</b>: 10<br /> <b>Essence</b>: 20<br /> <b>Initiative</b>: 15<br /> <b>Defense</b>: 6<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 20<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5<br /> <b>Corpus:</b> 11<br /> <b>Influences:</b> Commerce 5<br /> <b>Manifestations</b>: Twilight Form, Discorporate, Reaching, Shadow Gateway<br /> <b>Numina</b>: Drain, Innocuous, Pathfinder, Seek; 2 Numina exchanged for Influence dots<br /> <b>Ban</b>: Palisades must must ensure that all advertising and promotions related to the mall remain upbeat and appealing.<br /> <b>Bane</b>: Obsolete commercial media. This includes, but is not limited to, physical objects like old-fashioned advertising materials (e.g., vintage billboards or brochures), obsolete technology (like old cash registers or outdated mall directories), or even digital artifacts representing past commercial trends.\u200b<br /> <b>Totem Advantage</b>: Merit: Pack Dynamics 5, Merit: Residential Area 5","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 09-15-2024, 08:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-25T19:29:37-07:00","id":1523157,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:24px\"><b>5 - \u2018Water Tribe\u2019 Pack</b></span><br /> <br /> The Water Tribe is an independent pack, located in Nunavut, Canada, near the North Pole. Composed of humans and wolf-blooded of Inuit heritage, they have been favoured by Luna herself who allowed them to have a Lune totem. The tribe has build an impressive Ice City (it is not fully ice, but almost), using their Totem granted powers to deal with the harsh climate and unfavourable conditions of the region.<br /> <br /> <b>Pack Aspirations:</b><br /> Short-Term \u2013 Improve the Ice City infrastructure.<br /> Medium-Term \u2013 Rejoin Northern and Southern Tribe members.<br /> Long-Term \u2013 Expand the population of the Tribe.<br /> <br /> <b>Pack Touchstones:</b><br /> Physical \u2013 The Ice City.<br /> Spiritual \u2013 The Spirit Oasis.<br /> <br /> <b>Pack Complications:</b><br /> Schism \u2013 The tribe population is divided between the Traditionalist, who inhabit the Ice City, and the Modernists based on the southern regions of Nunavut. The division was caused by an inability to agree on certain social and cultural practices. Now that the general population is declining, the time to merge both sets of people has arrived.<br /> Dual Spirits \u2013 Tui is their Totem, but its companion Lu is also part of the pack. The problem is that Lu does not have the same concern for the Pack well being as Tui, and when defending the Spirit Oasis it might not show restraint for the humans.<br /> <br /> <b>Hunting Nature: </b><br /> Human<br /> <br /> <b>Pack Merits:</b><br /> Dedicated Locus 5<br /> Magnanimous Totem 4<br /> Moon\u2019s Grace 3<br /> Safe Place 5<br /> Territorial Advantage 5<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Totem: Tui, Pushing Moon</b></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Totem Type:</b> Lune<br /> <b>Totem Rank: </b>3<br /> <b>Background: </b>Reportedly &quot;near the beginning of time&quot;, Tui and La chose to manifest themselves in the mortal world to benefit mankind and took up residence together as koi fish in a locus, the Spirit Oasis.<br /> <br /> <b>Description: </b>A white koi fish with a large black spot on its head.<br /> <br /> <b>Storytelling Hints:</b> If it was not obvious enough this is a blatant copy of the Waterbending Tribes in <i>Avatar the Last Airbender</i>. I tried to be as close to the details as possible while still being set in the Chronicles of Darkness. Feel free to modify.<br /> <br /> <b>Aspirations: </b>Protect the Spirit Oasis.<br /> <br /> <b>Totem Points:</b> 21<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Rank</b>: 3<br /> <b>Attributes</b>: Power 9, Finesse 9, Resistance 3<br /> <b>Willpower</b>: 10<br /> <b>Essence</b>: 20<br /> <b>Initiative</b>: 12<br /> <b>Defense</b>: 9<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 18 ground / 28 swim<br /> <b>Size:</b> 3<br /> <b>Corpus:</b> 6<br /> <b>Influences:</b> Health 2, Ice 1, Moonlight 3, Water 3<br /> <b>Manifestations</b>: Twilight Form, Fetter, Possess, Claim<br /> <b>Numina</b>: 6 Numina exchanged for Influence dots<br /> <b>Ban</b>: Tui must disrupt the pack bond during a lunar eclipse, the pack loses access to the totem and any advantages during this time. Tui can only accept descendants of the Water tribe as members of the pack.<br /> <b>Bane</b>: Fire created by supernatural sources.<br /> <b>Conditions: </b>Fettered (Spirit Oasis)\u200b<br /> <b>Totem Advantage</b>: Merit: Psychokinetic Resistance (Cryokinesis), Merit: Psychokinesis (Cryokinesis) 5, Merit: Shadow Occultism (taboo: can only learn Influences or supernatural merits associated with Healing or Water)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Spirit: La, Pulling Ocean</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Spirit Type:</b> Oceanic Spirit<br /> <br /> <b>Description: </b>A black koi fish with a large white spot on its head.\u200b<br /> <br /> <b>Rank</b>: 3<br /> <b>Attributes</b>: Power 9, Finesse 9, Resistance 3<br /> <b>Willpower</b>: 10<br /> <b>Essence</b>: 20<br /> <b>Initiative</b>: 12<br /> <b>Defense</b>: 9<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 18 ground / 28 swim<br /> <b>Size:</b> 3<br /> <b>Corpus:</b> 6<br /> <b>Influences:</b> Light 1, Ice 2, Tides 3, Water 3<br /> <b>Manifestations</b>: Twilight Form, Fetter, Possess, Claim<br /> <b>Numina</b>: 6 Numina exchanged for Influence dots<br /> <b>Ban</b>: La can only claim live humans with a supernatural template.<br /> <b>Bane</b>: Fire created by supernatural sources.\u200b<br /> <b>Conditions: </b>Fettered (Spirit Oasis)\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 09-15-2024, 09:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-10T14:53:02-07:00","id":1534002,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Not a full pack concept, but a pretty nifty totem idea I wanted to share. </span></span>This may or may not have sprung from a particularly weird dream <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I recently had.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Flesh Cradle </span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Instead of worn tile, there\u2019s a thick layer of seemingly human skin veiling the interior surfaces of the hot tub. It gently pulsates as if breathing through some unseen orifice. Undefinable muscles begin undulating beneath the surface. The flesh swells and parts, tendrils extended as if for an embrace. Enter, it beckons. Be made whole. Never be alone and broken again.</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Concept</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Rejuvenation through visceral rebirth.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Aspiration</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Render whole all flesh</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Description</b>: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Flesh Cradle has long feasted on feelings of healing, life, renewal, and the dysphoria of a body changed, reconstructed, forever altered. It acts as a sort of reverse scavenger, trailing those who leave broken, mutilated flesh in their wake, so it can offer its embrace to those surviving violent encounters. Thus it\u2019s no surprise that it may willingly offer itself as Totem to Uratha packs. In addition to an ever fresh supply of potential \u201cchildren\u201d, the Cradle is fascinated by the mercurial flesh of Luna\u2019s children. The pack members in turn receive the Cradle\u2019s prodigious healing gifts, allowing them to conserve Essence and recover from injuries even their inhuman metabolisms cannot otherwise easily mend. Experiencing the rapture of the embrace is just a fringe benefit.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When the Cradle embraces an organism, its corpus merges with the subject\u2019s flesh, filling in wounds, purging toxins, stimulating regrowth. It claims these subject\u2019s as its own, joined together like mother and child. The Cradle prefers to fully envelope its subjects, but with sufficient cajoling or offerings, it will be willing to merely embrace the part of the subject that needs reconstruction. However, it always extends the offer for the subject to remain, to become truly one with the Fleshy Cradle. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The experience of being released from the embrace can also be rather unsettling. The subject must \u201cpeel\u201d themselves free from what was, temporarily, an extension of their own flesh. This takes no small amount of constitution. Subjects requiring extensive reconstruction or replacement body parts will not emerge quite the same as before; the spirit is versed in what the human body is supposed to look like and how it functions, but is a bit hazy on individual variation. Those released after an extended embrace are essentially born anew when they are finally expelled. If they ever emerge at all; those who approached the Cradle in violence are not afforded that privilege. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Cradle does not speak, not with words, but in a more intimate and visceral manner. While in physical contact, a creature perceives the Cradle\u2019s intent as a trickle of sensation, a rush of hormones, speaking directly to primal reflex rather than higher consciousness. A successful Empathy+Stamina roll may be required to interpret the nuances of these communications. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Totem Points</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: 15</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Rank</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: 3</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Attributes</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Power 5, Finesse 5, Resistance 5</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Willpower</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: 10</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Essence</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: 15</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Initiative</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: 10</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Defense</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: 5</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Speed</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: 1</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Size</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: 10</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Corpus</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: 15</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Influences</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Flesh 3</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Manifestations</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Gauntlet Breach, Materialize, Reaching, Shadow Gate</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Numina</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Fleshy Embrace, Rapture, Regenerate</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Ban</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: If the Cradle has not embraced at least one creature in the last week, it cannot regain Essence until it does so. Pack members must spend a number of hours in its embrace per week equal to their dots in the Totem merit. Other pack members can make up for another member\u2019s lapse for a week before the Ban is considered violated.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Bane</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Temperatures and substances cold enough to damage flesh on contact.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Totem Advantage</b>: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Merit: Biokinesis (Chronicles of Darkness pg 57) at five dots. For Uratha, increase the amount of bashing damage healed per round by 1, instead of doubling it. Normal healing times for lethal and aggravate damage are still halved.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">New Numina - Fleshy Embrace (R)</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: The Flesh Cradle may embrace any organic creature within its walls. Against an unwilling subject, the Flesh Cradle must make a grappling maneuver following a successful grapple attempt. The creature is then immobilized within the spirit\u2019s corpus. Breaking free (whether the embrace was voluntary or not) requires 3 successes on an extended Strength+Resolve roll (roll once per round), potentially contested by the Cradle\u2019s Power+Resistance. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Once embraced, a bleeding creature stops losing health. The embrace provides the equivalent of intensive medical care, rolling the Cradle\u2019s Power+Finesse in place of Intelligence+Medicine, and with no limit on the number of wounds it can downgrade per day. Additionally, embraced creatures double their natural healing rate, and can regenerate body parts or otherwise fully recover from physical injuries and Tilts that would normally be permanent. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Cradle pays one less Essence to use Influences and Numina on those it embraces, and can embrace up to four size 5 creatures at a time.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Embraced creatures lose their Defense against all attacks.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mortals suffer a breaking point with each embrace. It is a breaking point towards spirit for Uratha with a Harmony of 8 or higher. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When used with the Reaching Manifestation, only a portion of the Cradle\u2019s corpus slips through the gauntlet, forming a sort of fleshy cocoon around the subject.</span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}